WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.500
<v Priya Shah>Hi Dr. Okafor, hi Lena, thanks for making time today.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
<v Maya Okafor>Of course. Lena runs the front office so I asked her to join.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.000
<v Lena Ortiz>Hi there.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Priya Shah>Great to have you both. So let me start by telling you a little about us. We work with practices across the region on patient acquisition, and we've built a system that answers every inquiry instantly, books appointments, and follows up automatically.

5
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Priya Shah>Our clients usually see more booked new patients in the first sixty days. We handle the ads, the follow-up, the reminders, and the reporting. You just show up and treat patients.

6
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.000
<v Maya Okafor>Okay. What made you reach out to us specifically?

7
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Priya Shah>You booked a call from our site, so I assume something isn't working the way you'd like. What's going on at the practice?

8
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Lena Ortiz>The phones are the big thing. We miss calls all day because the front desk is checking people in and out. By lunch there are six or seven voicemails and half of those people never call back.

9
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:16.000
<v Maya Okafor>And no-shows. We have a lot of no-shows on new patient exams, which kills the schedule.

10
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Priya Shah>That's exactly what our system fixes. It answers every call and text instantly, day or night, books the appointment, and sends reminders so the no-shows drop. Let me share my screen and show you the dashboard.

11
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:58.000
<v Priya Shah>So here you can see every lead, where it came from, and whether it booked. This practice is in a similar market to yours. They went from about twenty new patients a month to forty-five. And here's the reminder sequence, text, email, and a call the day before.

12
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:08.000
<v Maya Okafor>That looks nice. One thing I worry about though is HIPAA. Where does the patient information go and who can see it?

13
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:18.000
<v Priya Shah>Yes, everything is secure. We use enterprise grade tools and we work with lots of healthcare clients, so it's all handled.

14
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:23.000
<v Maya Okafor>Okay. Would you sign a business associate agreement?

15
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.000
<v Priya Shah>I'd have to check on that with our team, but I'm sure it's fine.

16
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:42.000
<v Lena Ortiz>The other thing is our patients are older. A lot of them are retirees. I don't think they'll like talking to a robot. They want a real person when they call a dentist.

17
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:52.000
<v Priya Shah>Honestly the AI is so good now that most people can't even tell. It sounds really natural.

18
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.000
<v Lena Ortiz>Hmm. I'm not sure that's what I'm worried about.

19
00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:08.000
<v Maya Okafor>We also have very few reviews online compared to the practice down the street, so people don't really know us.

20
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:20.000
<v Priya Shah>We can help with that too. We have a review request flow that goes out after every visit. So pricing is a one time setup of two thousand and then two thousand five hundred a month, on a twelve month agreement.

21
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:30.000
<v Maya Okafor>Twelve months is a long contract for something we haven't tried. Do you have anything month to month?

22
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:38.000
<v Priya Shah>The twelve months is really needed for the system to work, so that's our standard.

23
00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:48.000
<v Maya Okafor>Okay. Let me think about it and talk it over with Lena. Can you send me some information we can look at?

24
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:56.000
<v Priya Shah>Absolutely, I'll send over our deck and a case study. Feel free to reach out with any questions.

25
00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.000
<v Maya Okafor>Thanks Priya.

26
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.000
<v Priya Shah>Thank you both, have a great day.
